{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/105386-new-system-speculation","id":105386,"title":"New system speculation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-03T22:47:44-07:00","id":105386,"title":"New system speculation","content":"So time to discuss something that doesn't exist yet. I thought we might throw around some guesses about the new system.<br /> <br /> Ian has said that it will use dots and d10s. I'm pretty sure we will still see pools of dice based on the description.<br /> <br /> I think we will still see some kind of Attribute+Ability system. Maybe different Attributes/Abilities, maybe a different number of them, but I think the combo is too useful to just drop.<br /> <br /> The big thing I think is the combat system. I've heard nWoD's combat system ddescribed a a &quot;murder machine&quot;, and I don't think that's what we want here. For a horror setting, nWoD's combat setting works well, being relatively short, brutal and lethal. Trinity Continuum is action movies, superheroes, pulp adventures and sci-fi action, and Scion is also somewhat upbeat. So here we might want a less immediately lethal style of combat system, maybe something that rewards risk taking. I'd even suggest something like a reverse death-spiral, but that might be too much to hope for. The game needs some lethality of course, for tension, but hopefully not too much.<br /> <br /> Any on have a ny thoughts? Maybe anything you'd like to see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T01:44:23-07:00","id":105441,"title":"","content":"Me? I\u2019d like something like <b>Seventh Sea</b>\u2019s Drama Dice, <b>Fate</b>\u2019s Fate Points, or <b>Cortex Plus</b>\u2019 Plot Points as an integral part of the system, available to all player characters. A limited and explicitly metagame resource that can be used to help your character literally cheat the odds when it would suit the genre conventions to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T02:22:52-07:00","id":105455,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of hoping, as far as combat goes, that the Trinity and Scion writers are looking at Ex3 a bit. The combat previews for Ex3 have a very good idea regarding meshing the horror genre origins of the ST system with a more cinematic action genre feel. Basically most combat actions are about gaining &quot;momentum&quot; or causing opponents to lose it. When you feel you have a big enough gap in momentum, you get to go for big fight ending hits, and if you're right you probably end the fight. But if you're wrong it could result in a reversal.<br /> <br /> Obviously there's a lot of wait and see on that idea with Ex3 not done yet, but it seems like a design framework that would benefit the Trinity rules just fine.<br /> <br /> As far as Dataweaver's point, I'd love to see Adventure!'s Inspiration/Dramatic Editing rules fill that role (though, biased, Adventure! is my favorite of the line). That is its entire purpose, and it doesn't seem that hard to make it integral to the whole game line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T03:47:36-07:00","id":105477,"title":"","content":"I remember hearing awhile back ago that the dramatic editing mechanic was going to be worked into all three settings but the line was dropped before it could be implemented. So, I think they may put it in. I would also like to see something akin to the Exalted stunt dice mechanic tossed into it as well. It is a great thing that really encourages players to think more dramatically. In the Scion game I run and the Exalted games I play in, anytime dice are brought in, we are always thinking of how to stunt the action even if it is for one more dice. As a result, we never do a &quot;I hit him&quot; and it ends up with us having awesome scenes in most cases.<br /> I think the combat momentum idea is a great one and, if it works as advertised, brings the feel of action movies to games. Something that it needs. I love the Aeoniverse and my players know that I will put whatever game we have going on at the time on hold and I will be running Aeoniverse for them...lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T06:20:00-07:00","id":105540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/105386-new-system-speculation?p=105455#post105455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kind of hoping, as far as combat goes, that the Trinity and Scion writers are looking at Ex3 a bit. The combat previews for Ex3 have a very good idea regarding meshing the horror genre origins of the ST system with a more cinematic action genre feel. Basically most combat actions are about gaining &quot;momentum&quot; or causing opponents to lose it. When you feel you have a big enough gap in momentum, you get to go for big fight ending hits, and if you're right you probably end the fight. But if you're wrong it could result in a reversal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m curious how this works for anything larger than a one-on-one duel. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/105386-new-system-speculation?p=105455#post105455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Dataweaver's point, I'd love to see Adventure!'s Inspiration/Dramatic Editing rules fill that role (though, biased, Adventure! is my favorite of the line). That is its entire purpose, and it doesn't seem that hard to make it integral to the whole game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dramatic Editing is certainly something I\u2019d want to be part of the \u201cdramatic currency\u201d system. But I\u2019m also talking about being able to use it to do things like converting dice into successes (e.g., spend one drama point to convert two dice into one automatic success) when attempting the sorts of dramatic feats that pulps, superheroes, space opera heroes, and (where <b>Scion</b> is concerned, since they\u2019re using a variant of the same game engine) heroes of myth and legend attempt: feats that a tactician would reject as foolhardy, but which the hero should embrace.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T07:42:13-07:00","id":105568,"title":"","content":"We haven't seen a lot out of Ex3's combat rules, so I have no idea how the Exalted team is using the concept in uneven numbers of combatants. I can imagine some solutions (ex: being outnumbers makes it easier to protect your momentum so ganging up on someone makes it harder to beat them allowing for both better &quot;boss fights&quot; without having to artificially inflate stats, and encouraging fighters to &quot;pair off&quot; in large fights rather than focus fire on one enemy at a time) but until we get more from Ex3 it is really hard to tell.<br /> <br /> My one concern with dramatic currency options and innate/default powers you can spend it on, is that if you go too far with it you end up taking away design space from purchased powers. Obviously some baseline meta-boosts are good (Legend in Scion did this just fine). But I don't want to see early entry powers feel like speed bumps because anyone could have just spent meta-points to do the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T07:55:21-07:00","id":105576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/105386-new-system-speculation?p=105540#post105540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m curious how this works for anything larger than a one-on-one duel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not mentioned as yet, only that it _does_ work smoothly for such situations, though it took a bit of initial tinkering to get right.<br /> <br /> We know that when fighting something like a horde of bandits or ninja, they're represented as a battle group, and damage to the battle group is considered to consist of incapacitated/dead members of the group, and loss of morale among the survivors rendering them less than useful. We don't know how the momentum thing works here, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:59:23-07:00","id":105715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/105386-new-system-speculation?p=105568#post105568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My one concern with dramatic currency options and innate/default powers you can spend it on, is that if you go too far with it you end up taking away design space from purchased powers. Obviously some baseline meta-boosts are good (Legend in Scion did this just fine). But I don't want to see early entry powers feel like speed bumps because anyone could have just spent meta-points to do the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a legitimate concern.<br /> <br /> I like &quot;dramatic currency&quot; in a fight, but if Inspiration points or whatever are going to replace health, I want them to genuinely replace health entirely. Exalted had health, but for 90% of the fights the important thing is Essence - run out of Essence and your Health Levels are basically tissue to be blown through. I don't want opponents pinging each other down - to me, that's dull. I want solid hits. <br /> <br /> The thing about momentum, is it's really just a different version of death spiral though - the fight starts going your way, then it keeps going your way. Sudden reversals, which are dramatically interesting, don't happen, and if your opponent starts winning, well, it's over. What I want to see is opponents getting more dangerous when hurt, rather than less. Heroes pull out their reserve of inner strength. Villains get desperate, and stop playing around. Wounded monsters turn vicious. That kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T12:46:01-07:00","id":105757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/105386-new-system-speculation?p=105715#post105715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about momentum, is it's really just a different version of death spiral though -the fight starts going your way, then it keeps going your way.<b> Sudden reversals, which are dramatically interesting, don't happen</b>, and if your opponent starts winning, well, it's over. What I want to see is opponents getting more dangerous when hurt, rather than less. Heroes pull out their reserve of inner strength. Villains get desperate, and stop playing around. Wounded monsters turn vicious. That kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>May I ask where you got that information? Because from what little is known so far, everything indicates that EX3's combat system was designed so that such reversals <b>do </b>happen.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:21:59-07:00","id":105784,"title":"","content":"I'm also not convinced that reverse spirals as the default is an inherently good idea. It seems much more like a situational thing. It sort of plays into my &quot;taking away design space for powers&quot; concern. I'd rather see something like a reverse spiral or no spiral be something some characters have to highlight their dramatic purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T14:59:23-07:00","id":105849,"title":"","content":"I'd like a combat system with a hard edge to it, an element of pseudo-realism over dramaticism.<br /> <br /> I always felt that Aberrant benefitted from that, as it was a game which did not take a &quot;the hero wins, because he truly believes!&quot; atittude towards superpowers, but rather a harsher &quot;the hero wins because he is powerful enough and clever enough that he can plausibly kick the crap out of the villain.&quot; If being the protaganist makes you inherently more capable, then that kind of goes against the themes of the game IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T23:29:19-07:00","id":106067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/105386-new-system-speculation?p=105784#post105784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also not convinced that reverse spirals as the default is an inherently good idea. It seems much more like a situational thing. It sort of plays into my &quot;taking away design space for powers&quot; concern. I'd rather see something like a reverse spiral or no spiral be something some characters have to highlight their dramatic purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be super-easy to bake powers into such a system, and would make sense as a baseline assumption when so many of the people involved in fights in game are going to be exceptional individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T12:07:46-07:00","id":107015,"title":"","content":"I've been playing a fair bit of Aberrant recently, and I feel that the although I don't really have a problem with the system as is, the combat system could do with being a bit more &quot;superhero-ey.&quot; I would like to see the ability to make dramatic fight scenes reasonably long and OTT, but still giving the players a feeling that they are getting somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T18:35:12-07:00","id":215398,"title":"","content":"I hope they bake the Gadgeteering rules into the Aberrant corebook. My favorite characters are definitely ones with Mega-Mental Attributes who build powered armor suits like Doctor Doom or Tony Stark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T20:07:28-07:00","id":215464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/105386-new-system-speculation?p=105455#post105455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kind of hoping, as far as combat goes, that the Trinity and Scion writers are looking at Ex3 a bit. The combat previews for Ex3 have a very good idea regarding meshing the horror genre origins of the ST system with a more cinematic action genre feel. Basically most combat actions are about gaining &quot;momentum&quot; or causing opponents to lose it. When you feel you have a big enough gap in momentum, you get to go for big fight ending hits, and if you're right you probably end the fight. But if you're wrong it could result in a reversal.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have not. The new system's development is running concurrently with Exalted's, though they have something of a head start. And, hey, different systems: even if we were to look at it, there isn't much we could adopt without heavy modification. Additionally, we have a number of base assumptions different from Storyteller.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, some of the elements that have been revealed, such as Charms working as extensions of your skill, seem to be along the same lines as things we're doing (though ours is a function of the dice mechanic and how actions work, and I don't know how Charms work in the new system).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as Dataweaver's point, I'd love to see Adventure!'s Inspiration/Dramatic Editing rules fill that role (though, biased, Adventure! is my favorite of the line). That is its entire purpose, and it doesn't seem that hard to make it integral to the whole game line. </div> </div> </div>Dramatic Editing has a pretty explicit role in both Trinity and Scion, and is a core mechanic as such.<br /> <br /> I will talk more about the system at Gen Con, probably, likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T13:18:52-07:00","id":216110,"title":"","content":"Any chance you'll be touching on the lethality and/or granularity of the system? One of my major sticking points with supers games is characters who can juggle tanks but don't kill normal humans with a punch (M&amp;M I'm looking at you). This is especially relevant in a game about the realistic consequences of god like powers, such as Aberrant. On the flip side, I love the granularity and the way ranks and measures are handled in the crunchier systems and hope to see more of that with the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3631-adamrice","name":"AdamRice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T12:17:34-07:00","id":216816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamRice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/105386-new-system-speculation?p=216110#post216110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance you'll be touching on the lethality and/or granularity of the system? One of my major sticking points with supers games is characters who can juggle tanks but don't kill normal humans with a punch (M&amp;M I'm looking at you). This is especially relevant in a game about the realistic consequences of god like powers, such as Aberrant. On the flip side, I love the granularity and the way ranks and measures are handled in the crunchier systems and hope to see more of that with the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I can touch on lethality at Gen Con. We've got a pretty decent system set up to handle scaling of power, I think. (actually, 3-4 systems, depending on what you want to tweak)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T12:59:45-07:00","id":216833,"title":"","content":"The most important of which is whether or not the player is capable of beating up the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T18:40:49-07:00","id":217101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/105386-new-system-speculation?p=216833#post216833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most important of which is whether or not the player is capable of beating up the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our chief dice-resolution mechanic is centered around pointy dice!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T20:41:56-07:00","id":217139,"title":"","content":"Carpe DM, eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T02:36:08-07:00","id":217266,"title":"","content":"Sounds great, I'm looking forward to hearing more. Finally, the arm-wrestling based resolution mechanic the gaming community has been clamoring for!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3631-adamrice","name":"AdamRice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T16:08:01-07:00","id":224580,"title":"","content":"Im hoping for more info on how to make or advance trinity era biotech. Currently im running an Adventure! game set in that time and am using the adventure super science abilities on the tech in the old trinity books. Biotech is supposed to be much harder to &quot;evolve&quot; I believe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T09:39:58-07:00","id":225117,"title":"","content":"The problem is that Biotech comes from templates provided by the Doyen; humanity did not invent it, and any advances it makes has its roots in the original templates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T10:54:45-07:00","id":225161,"title":"","content":"I rhought there was a reason biotech was tough to &quot;edit&quot;. The qin are blown away by what humanity can do with biotech, but it all stems from the doyen? I thought the levia ships were, while not wholly understood, a human concept...or more so a psion concept. <br /> Side question-would you say that biotech would require super science engineering, medical, science, or a combo of two of those to be upgraded/worked on? I was thinking that biotech would require super medicine, but also a correlating say 3 or better in engineering to attempt advancement/innovation .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T11:20:40-07:00","id":225174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/105386-new-system-speculation?p=225161#post225161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rhought there was a reason biotech was tough to &quot;edit&quot;. The qin are blown away by what humanity can do with biotech, but it all stems from the doyen? I thought the levia ships were, while not wholly understood, a human concept...or more so a psion concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have this backwards. The Qin are the ones who are amazing at biotech. They don't have hardtech itself. Even biotech items made by humans tend to have a little bit of a hardtech element, whereas everything the Qin use is grown. Also, the Leviathan ships were only possible to make by the Psions in conjunction with the Qin. Their help was requisite.<br /> <br /> However, the Qin don't have access to Psi, much less Quantum, so humanity's integration and research in those directions do impress the Qin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T11:47:08-07:00","id":225188,"title":"","content":"Right, right, now I remember. The qin have low level instinctive psychic abilities but are amazed at humanities power with psionics, but they grow Everything. Yep, had it backwards, lol. Well then...in the reboot, I would like to see what humanity can do with the qin and without the artificial barriers of the doyen (prometheus chambers blocking access to only one power tree)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T22:37:57-07:00","id":267212,"title":"","content":"Alright so the spoilers so far seem to indicate a psi power system that will be both more flexible than the original baseline psi system, but not as complicated as the system from the Player's Guide. Comparisons were made to Bloody Magic from vampire in terms of versatility. I'm not sure how I feel about this because Blood Magic is one of my least favorite subsystems in any WW/OP game, but hey, it's only a rough analogy.<br /> <br /> So, from that, I'm thinking of a few possibilities.<br /> <br /> 1) You have a cafeteria of powers, and you have access to a number of them based on your rating in your Aptitude/Modes. So at 1 dot I get 1 power, say, lifting things psychokinetically, and then at the next dot I get to pick another. Could be one per level, or several per level, or more as level goes up or even fewer as level goes up, depending.<br /> <br /> 2) You get a suite of powers every level. So each dot has three or four (or more) things it can do, and you can freely use these abilities.<br /> <br /> 3) You have a number of abilities that just get better as dots in Aptitude/Mode go up. So all telekinetics can fly, it's just you need several dots before it's really impressive, but at low levels you could counteract gravity to a degree. <br /> <br /> 4) Some combination of the above.<br /> <br /> I think they are going to stay away from powers having requisites of each other for the most part because I think there is enough proof that doesn't really work well in an RPG, and wouldn't be elegant game design (maybe they pull it off though, who knows).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}